From 642064b1ff240214e79b14efbc7da3694e1bdef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:16:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] Vizzbox: the producer (generators, arrangement, voice
 budget) and its renderer

firmware/src/producer.c, producer_isr.c, producer_tables.c: a song from genre, subgenre, seed, energy,
variation and length; generators for drums, bass, chords, lead, arp and FX; the arrangement in sections
with an energy curve; each bar written in the main loop one bar ahead into launch_q (LOOP), the ISR
applying each step's prepared control (tempo, filter, FX layer, CC 104..109). Every part draws from its
own stream of the seed: the same song is the same bytes. The voice budget (8) is kept per step from the
sounds' measured rings and tails, the swing and ratchets included, with room for the next bar's kick and
bass. The GROOVEBOX's music waits packed in RAM (.vbox after .bss, app.ld) while the producer plays;
the autosave, the pattern pool and SONG leave its tracks alone. firmware/src/ui_vizzbox.c: a first
VIZZBOX screen and its controls.

tools/vizzbox_render.c: a whole song as the unit plays it, to WAV and a Standard MIDI File.
tools/vizzbox_sounds.c, vizzbox_sounds.py, vizzbox_pick.py: every factory sound rendered and measured
in every role; the producer's sound lists chosen from the measurements.

tools/size_fns.py: the producer built for size (minsize) like the rest of the main loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawnvCsrvDZVbc37ZFUY
